{
  "_comment": "WTF-520: clicks and input changes of the page's own elements in repeating group cells. A list of products whose row button shows that product in a detail group outside the list (master-detail), a quantity input per row whose change writes that row's product, a row button whose workflow is not lowered (the refusal notice), and a nested list (categories, then each category's products) whose row button shows the product and its category. All data invented; test/support/target/phoenix/cell_clicks_behavior.exs runs it. A reusable product picker (its own list, a row's button showing the row's product in a group of the picker) is on the products page and in each category's cell; a row's Later button pauses before it shows its product.",
  "_id": "cell-clicks-fixture",
